1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,566
Silver rings, chains and earrings turn
dull and

2
00:00:03,576 --> 00:00:05,003
dark with time.

3
00:00:05,457 --> 00:00:06,884
You don't need a jeweler.

4
00:00:08,034 --> 00:00:11,716
Seven steps, three simple ways to remove
tarnish

5
00:00:11,726 --> 00:00:15,838
at home, with soap, baking soda and
aluminum

6
00:00:15,848 --> 00:00:16,532
foil.

7
00:00:17,682 --> 00:00:20,630
Twenty minutes, almost no cost.

8
00:00:21,432 --> 00:00:24,638
Stay for step four: the tarnish lifts off

9
00:00:24,648 --> 00:00:26,157
without any rubbing.

10
00:00:26,767 --> 00:00:27,823
WikiTube.

11
00:00:28,114 --> 00:00:32,212
Whatever it is, here's how.

12
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,427
Silver tarnishes when it reacts with
sulfur in

13
00:00:35,437 --> 00:00:38,920
the air, in food, even on your skin.

14
00:00:39,884 --> 00:00:43,761
It's only a thin surface layer, and it
comes off.

15
00:00:44,726 --> 00:00:47,836
A gentle wash is safe for almost
everything;

16
00:00:48,290 --> 00:00:52,759
stronger methods are only for solid silver
without delicate stones.

17
00:00:53,212 --> 00:00:57,449
Never clean a valuable heirloom without
asking a jeweler first.

18
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,437
You'll need mild dish soap and warm water,

19
00:01:00,496 --> 00:01:04,791
baking soda, aluminum foil, a soft
toothbrush,

20
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:06,893
and a silver polishing cloth.

21
00:01:07,184 --> 00:01:10,272
Use a glass or ceramic bowl for the hot
water.

22
00:01:10,833 --> 00:01:11,854
Step one.

23
00:01:12,215 --> 00:01:14,188
Look closely at each piece.

24
00:01:14,641 --> 00:01:18,959
Is it solid sterling silver, often stamped
925,

25
00:01:19,193 --> 00:01:20,527
or silver-plated?

26
00:01:21,073 --> 00:01:23,560
Plating is a thin layer that can wear

27
00:01:23,570 --> 00:01:25,391
away with harsh rubbing.

28
00:01:26,054 --> 00:01:30,142
Check for gemstones, pearls, opals,
turquoise

29
00:01:30,152 --> 00:01:33,544
or glued parts, because soft or porous
stones

30
00:01:33,554 --> 00:01:36,618
are damaged by soaking and strong methods.

31
00:01:37,281 --> 00:01:41,564
Antique pieces with dark detail, called
oxidized silver,

32
00:01:41,623 --> 00:01:43,921
are meant to look dark in the crevices,

33
00:01:43,945 --> 00:01:45,325
so don't remove it.

34
00:01:45,872 --> 00:01:48,750
If you're unsure, stick to method one.

35
00:01:49,413 --> 00:01:51,400
If a piece has a clasp or hinge

36
00:01:51,410 --> 00:01:54,555
that moves, test that it works before
cleaning,

37
00:01:54,684 --> 00:01:56,866
and check again afterwards.

38
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:58,525
Step two.

39
00:01:59,188 --> 00:02:02,521
This safe, gentle method works for light
tarnish

40
00:02:02,531 --> 00:02:03,947
and everyday dirt.

41
00:02:04,308 --> 00:02:07,314
Fill a bowl with warm, not boiling, water,

42
00:02:07,373 --> 00:02:09,984
and add a few drops of mild dish soap.

43
00:02:10,531 --> 00:02:13,470
Soak your jewelry for five minutes, then
gently

44
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:16,848
scrub with a soft toothbrush, paying
attention to

45
00:02:16,858 --> 00:02:18,970
the chain links and the settings.

46
00:02:19,633 --> 00:02:22,987
Rinse under lukewarm water and pat dry.

47
00:02:23,650 --> 00:02:26,241
Close the sink drain first, so a small

48
00:02:26,251 --> 00:02:27,922
ring can't disappear.

49
00:02:28,468 --> 00:02:30,664
Always dry your hands and the piece well

50
00:02:30,674 --> 00:02:34,031
afterwards, so that no soap film stays
behind

51
00:02:34,041 --> 00:02:35,410
to dull the shine.

52
00:02:36,561 --> 00:02:39,290
If some tarnish is still there, the next

53
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:41,575
method goes one step further.

54
00:02:42,133 --> 00:02:43,200
Step three.

55
00:02:43,654 --> 00:02:46,999
For moderate tarnish, mix three parts
baking soda

56
00:02:47,009 --> 00:02:49,969
with one part water to make a thick paste.

57
00:02:50,202 --> 00:02:52,305
Apply it with a soft cloth or your

58
00:02:52,315 --> 00:02:55,881
fingertip, and rub gently along the piece,
following

59
00:02:55,891 --> 00:02:57,910
the direction of any grain.

60
00:02:58,875 --> 00:03:03,857
Baking soda is a mild abrasive,

61
00:03:03,867 --> 00:03:07,941
so it removes tarnish without scratching
sterling silver much.

62
00:03:08,395 --> 00:03:10,890
Use a soft toothbrush for detail.

63
00:03:11,251 --> 00:03:14,396
Rinse well, and dry with a soft cloth.

64
00:03:15,198 --> 00:03:18,727
Don't use this method on plated silver or
soft stones.

65
00:03:19,088 --> 00:03:21,609
Do a small test spot first, just in

66
00:03:21,619 --> 00:03:24,836
case, and keep the pressure light, since
silver

67
00:03:24,846 --> 00:03:26,215
is a soft metal.

68
00:03:26,767 --> 00:03:27,846
Step four.

69
00:03:28,648 --> 00:03:31,332
For heavy tarnish on solid silver, line a

70
00:03:31,342 --> 00:03:35,776
glass or ceramic bowl with aluminum foil,
shiny side up.

71
00:03:36,438 --> 00:03:39,514
Place the silver on the foil, so it
touches.

72
00:03:40,061 --> 00:03:42,500
Add one tablespoon of baking soda per cup

73
00:03:42,510 --> 00:03:44,904
of very hot water, and pour it over

74
00:03:44,914 --> 00:03:46,701
the jewelry until covered.

75
00:03:47,363 --> 00:03:48,524
It will fizz.

76
00:03:49,186 --> 00:03:51,742
Wait two to five minutes, and the tarnish

77
00:03:51,752 --> 00:03:53,260
transfers to the foil.

78
00:03:53,807 --> 00:03:56,700
This method uses a chemical reaction, and
it

79
00:03:56,710 --> 00:03:58,497
has a slight sulfur smell.

80
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:01,623
Take care with hot water, and never leave

81
00:04:01,633 --> 00:04:04,685
it unattended with children or pets
nearby.

82
00:04:05,139 --> 00:04:07,785
Let the water cool before pouring it away.

83
00:04:08,935 --> 00:04:13,218
Now for the part most people rush: rinsing
and drying.

84
00:04:13,767 --> 00:04:14,892
Step five.

85
00:04:15,125 --> 00:04:17,634
Remove the pieces from the water with
tongs

86
00:04:17,644 --> 00:04:20,302
or a spoon, since they will be hot.

87
00:04:21,452 --> 00:04:24,391
Rinse each piece under cool running water
to

88
00:04:24,401 --> 00:04:26,142
remove all residue.

89
00:04:27,292 --> 00:04:31,517
Dry with a soft cotton or microfiber cloth
immediately.

90
00:04:32,668 --> 00:04:35,142
Moisture left in the links or the settings

91
00:04:35,152 --> 00:04:37,311
can bring the tarnish back sooner.

92
00:04:37,857 --> 00:04:40,506
For chains, use a cloth to wipe gently

93
00:04:40,516 --> 00:04:41,641
along the length.

94
00:04:42,095 --> 00:04:45,031
If a spot remains dark, repeat the method,

95
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,924
rather than scrubbing harder.

96
00:04:47,888 --> 00:04:51,556
Pat, don't rub, near any delicate details.

97
00:04:52,103 --> 00:04:54,136
A hair dryer on a cool setting can

98
00:04:54,146 --> 00:04:56,038
help dry tricky links.

99
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:57,690
Step six.

100
00:04:58,051 --> 00:05:01,025
Use a silver polishing cloth, which is
treated

101
00:05:01,035 --> 00:05:04,275
with a mild polish and tarnish inhibitor,
to

102
00:05:04,285 --> 00:05:05,445
buff the piece.

103
00:05:05,899 --> 00:05:09,198
Rub gently, using long strokes, and turn
the

104
00:05:09,208 --> 00:05:12,330
cloth to a clean section when it becomes
dark.

105
00:05:12,993 --> 00:05:15,688
Do not use paper towels or tissues, which

106
00:05:15,698 --> 00:05:17,044
can leave scratches.

107
00:05:17,405 --> 00:05:20,678
Polish chains by pulling them through the
folded cloth.

108
00:05:21,340 --> 00:05:23,363
A few minutes of buffing brings out the

109
00:05:23,373 --> 00:05:26,228
brightness, and leaves a protective layer.

110
00:05:27,192 --> 00:05:29,365
Keep your cloth in a zip bag between

111
00:05:29,375 --> 00:05:32,613
uses, so it doesn't pick up dust or
moisture.

112
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:36,435
One thing is left: stopping the tarnish
from

113
00:05:36,445 --> 00:05:37,896
coming straight back.

114
00:05:38,433 --> 00:05:39,547
Step seven.

115
00:05:40,210 --> 00:05:44,435
Tarnish returns fastest when silver meets
air and moisture.

116
00:05:45,585 --> 00:05:48,800
Store each piece separately in a soft
pouch,

117
00:05:48,859 --> 00:05:51,981
or a small zip bag with the air pressed
out.

118
00:05:52,528 --> 00:05:55,105
Anti-tarnish bags or strips help.

119
00:05:56,255 --> 00:05:59,507
Keep silver away from bathrooms, and put
it

120
00:05:59,517 --> 00:06:03,673
on last, after perfume, hairspray and
lotion.

121
00:06:04,475 --> 00:06:07,715
Take it off before swimming, as chlorine
damages

122
00:06:07,725 --> 00:06:10,801
silver, and before cleaning or cooking.

123
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:14,472
Wearing silver often actually helps,
because your skin

124
00:06:14,482 --> 00:06:16,002
oils keep it polished.

125
00:06:16,363 --> 00:06:18,385
A small piece of chalk in the pouch

126
00:06:18,395 --> 00:06:22,980
also absorbs moisture, which helps your
silver stay bright longer.

127
00:06:23,533 --> 00:06:26,252
If the tarnish stays, check your setup
before

128
00:06:26,262 --> 00:06:27,410
you try again.

129
00:06:27,864 --> 00:06:30,699
The foil must touch the silver, the water

130
00:06:30,709 --> 00:06:33,090
must be very hot, and the piece must

131
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:34,411
be fully covered.

132
00:06:34,958 --> 00:06:37,235
Repeat the bath once, and use a soft

133
00:06:37,245 --> 00:06:38,916
toothbrush on the crevices.

134
00:06:39,277 --> 00:06:42,260
Do not scrub harder, because silver is
soft

135
00:06:42,284 --> 00:06:43,897
and scratches easily.

136
00:06:44,350 --> 00:06:47,208
If the piece is plated, stop, because thin

137
00:06:47,218 --> 00:06:48,900
plating can wear through.

138
00:06:49,467 --> 00:06:52,021
Some pieces are worth a visit to a
jeweler.

139
00:06:52,474 --> 00:06:56,168
Antiques and family heirlooms deserve a
professional's judgment

140
00:06:56,178 --> 00:06:58,267
before anything goes in water.

141
00:06:59,417 --> 00:07:03,831
Pearls, opals, turquoise and other soft
stones

142
00:07:03,841 --> 00:07:05,326
need special care.

143
00:07:05,872 --> 00:07:08,985
A jeweler can also tighten loose stones,
fix

144
00:07:08,995 --> 00:07:11,656
a weak clasp, and check the small metal

145
00:07:11,666 --> 00:07:14,173
prongs that hold a stone in place.

146
00:07:14,626 --> 00:07:18,642
Deep pitting or flaking plating needs a
jeweler's opinion.

147
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:21,930
Tarnish comes from sulfur in the air, and

148
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:23,553
your daily habits matter.

149
00:07:24,518 --> 00:07:28,246
Put on perfume, hairspray and lotion
before your

150
00:07:28,256 --> 00:07:30,148
jewelry, never after.

151
00:07:31,112 --> 00:07:34,573
Take silver off before swimming, because
chlorine can

152
00:07:34,583 --> 00:07:37,740
damage it, and before showering or
cleaning.

153
00:07:38,891 --> 00:07:41,528
Wiping each piece with a soft cloth after

154
00:07:41,538 --> 00:07:43,952
wearing removes oils and sweat.

155
00:07:45,102 --> 00:07:48,366
Keep silver away from rubber bands, wool
and

156
00:07:48,376 --> 00:07:50,976
eggs, which all contain sulfur.

157
00:07:51,533 --> 00:07:53,703
Here are the mistakes to avoid.

158
00:07:54,854 --> 00:07:58,826
First, using abrasive cleaners or
toothpaste, which scratch

159
00:07:58,836 --> 00:08:01,285
silver, and leave dull marks.

160
00:08:02,435 --> 00:08:06,779
Second, soaking pieces with pearls, opals,
turquoise

161
00:08:06,789 --> 00:08:08,262
or glued stones.

162
00:08:08,623 --> 00:08:10,770
They can crack or lose color.

163
00:08:11,433 --> 00:08:15,103
And third, cleaning oxidized or antique
silver the

164
00:08:15,113 --> 00:08:17,913
same way, which removes the dark detail
that

165
00:08:17,923 --> 00:08:19,164
gives it character.

166
00:08:20,129 --> 00:08:23,021
When in doubt, use soap and water, or

167
00:08:23,031 --> 00:08:24,133
ask a jeweler.

168
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:27,224
If you own valuable or antique silver, a

169
00:08:27,234 --> 00:08:29,950
jeweler is always the safest choice.

170
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:31,556
Let's recap.

171
00:08:31,917 --> 00:08:33,193
Check what you're cleaning.

172
00:08:34,158 --> 00:08:35,910
Start with soap and water.

173
00:08:36,201 --> 00:08:38,360
Move up to a baking soda paste.

174
00:08:38,651 --> 00:08:40,916
Use the foil and baking soda bath on

175
00:08:40,926 --> 00:08:42,493
solid silver only.

176
00:08:42,668 --> 00:08:44,548
Rinse and dry thoroughly.

177
00:08:45,698 --> 00:08:47,497
Polish with a silver cloth.

178
00:08:47,556 --> 00:08:50,237
And store your silver to slow down
tarnish.

179
00:08:51,201 --> 00:08:54,788
Seven steps, about twenty minutes, and
your silver

180
00:08:54,812 --> 00:08:56,042
will shine again.

181
00:08:57,192 --> 00:08:59,411
Bonus sections cover what to do if the

182
00:08:59,421 --> 00:09:02,674
tarnish stays, when to see a jeweler, and

183
00:09:02,684 --> 00:09:05,341
the daily habits that keep silver shining.

184
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:08,488
That's how you clean silver jewelry at
home

185
00:09:08,513 --> 00:09:10,509
with three easy methods.

186
00:09:10,962 --> 00:09:13,623
If your silver is shining again, subscribe
to

187
00:09:13,633 --> 00:09:18,020
WikiTube, because we publish a new how-to
every single day.

188
00:09:18,381 --> 00:09:20,066
Tell us in the comments which piece you

189
00:09:20,076 --> 00:09:23,257
cleaned, and what you would like us to
explain next.

190
00:09:24,407 --> 00:09:25,474
See you tomorrow.

191
00:09:25,835 --> 00:09:27,683
Share this with someone who has a drawer

192
00:09:27,693 --> 00:09:28,945
of dull silver.

193
00:09:29,033 --> 00:09:30,251
That's WikiTube.

194
00:09:30,542 --> 00:09:32,666
